<p>The United States has issued a 30-day sanctions waiver allowing the delivery and sale of Iranian crude oil and petroleum products loaded onto ships before March 20, with the authorization running through April 19. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the move is meant to get more oil onto the market after prices climbed above $100 a barrel following the recent U.S.-Israeli attack on Iran, Israeli strikes on Iran’s offshore gas field, and Iran’s closure of the Strait of Hormuz, which disrupted global energy supplies. The waiver is a limited, temporary easing within President Trump’s broader pressure campaign on Iran, not a full policy reversal. U.S. officials said it applies only to cargoes already at sea and argued Iran would have difficulty accessing much of the resulting revenue because broader sanctions and financial restrictions remain in place. For now, the step is a short-term effort to steady oil and gasoline markets as regional conflict continues and shipping risks remain unresolved.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_3J3BvvIo5Ff5L8YbTKYfcY2sNCcEWwRLMOvQooo1-_uIpZInOxwj4_pu4TXuPvVuW3I7bS7acV0UfYZLc4U0W_AFCYPYiH9phEf134T2LCI4xTnyzwT8swISpzQEndJ8kRJJtqjYv3EwMjv9boMRcRw9DXLm0uMITT0HCevA1Ba8hxLsGK5t2GHcJ2BT0aeJCoeqT4B-AT4MXiF2n8d__ziruU__Agw' alt='Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said Iran would see little economic benefit from the temporary removal of the sanctions.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Barrels unlocked: Bessent estimated the waiver could allow the sale of about 140 million barrels of Iranian oil already in transit.</li><li>Third waiver: This is the third time in a little more than two weeks that Washington has temporarily waived sanctions on oil from U.S. adversaries to ease supply pressure.</li><li>Buyer relief: The Treasury authorization shields buyers of eligible Iranian oil cargoes already at sea from sanctions penalties during the 30-day window.</li><li>Revenue limits: Bessent said Tehran would have difficulty accessing any revenue generated from the approved sales because broader financial restrictions remain in place.</li></ul><blockquote>In essence, we will be using the Iranian barrels against Tehran to keep the price down as we continue Operation Epic Fury - Scott Bessent</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent: Bessent described the waiver as a tactical step to calm markets, saying the U.S. would use Iranian barrels already at sea to bring prices down while keeping pressure on Tehran. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/20/us-pauses-sanctions-on-some-of-irans-oil-as-gas-prices-surge-00839109'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: Administration officials described the move as a temporary exemption for shipments already in transit, not a reopening of Iran’s oil trade, and stressed that long-standing restrictions on Iran’s oil industry otherwise remain in place. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-administration-temporarily-lifts-sanctions-on-iranian-oil-at-sea/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>New York Times analysis: The move was framed as a practical effort to cushion global energy markets, even though it partially reverses a sanctions regime Washington has long used to weaken Iran economically. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/middleeast/us-sanctions-iran-oil.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-us-pauses-sanctions-on-iranian-oil-at-sea-amid-soaring-prices-strait-of-hormuz-blockade-11245819#publisher=newsstand'>US Pauses Sanctions On Iranian Oil At Sea Amid Soaring Prices</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-issues-30-day-sanctions-waiver-for-sale-of-iranian-oil-at-sea/article70768207.ece'>U.S. issues 30-day sanctions waiver for sale of Iranian oil at sea</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/20/us-pauses-sanctions-on-some-of-irans-oil-as-gas-prices-surge-00839109'>US pauses sanctions on some of Iran’s oil as gas prices surge</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/middleeast/us-sanctions-iran-oil.html'>U.S. Pauses Sanctions on Some Iranian Oil to Get More to Market</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-administration-temporarily-lifts-sanctions-on-iranian-oil-at-sea/'>Trump administration temporarily lifts sanctions on Iranian oil at sea</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-issues-30-day-sanctions-waiver-for-sale-of-iranian-oil-at-sea'>US issues 30-day sanctions waiver for sale of Iranian oil at sea in bid to tame prices</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-authorizes-temporary-delivery-sale-oil-originating-iran'>US authorizes temporary delivery, sale of oil originating from Iran</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/economy-trade-business/article/3347401/us-approves-sale-iranian-oil-sea-move-ease-crude-supply-crisis'>US approves sale of Iranian oil at sea in move to ease crude supply crisis</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/20/us-sanctions-iranian-oil'>U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announces that the U.S. will temporary lift sanctions on Iranian oil at sea in a effort to ease energy supply pressures. The temporary relief will last for 30 days until April 19.</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>